==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|exquīsītus||to be outsought}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|exquīrō||I [[outseek]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-exquisite.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈskwɪzɪt/|/ˈɛkskwɪzɪt/|a=UK}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[specially|Specially]] [[fine]] or [[pleasing]]; [[exceptional]].
#: {{ux|en|They sell good coffee and pastries, but their chocolate is '''exquisite'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sourav Ganguly scored an '''exquisite''' century in his debut Test match.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|I|passage=Selwyn, sitting up rumpled and cross-legged on the floor, after having boloed Drina to everybody's '''exquisite''' satisfaction, looked around at the sudden rustle of skirts to catch a glimpse of a vanishing figure&mdash;a glimmer of ruddy hair and the white curve of a youthful face, half-buried in a muff.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=February 5, 1983
|title=Yingko -- Taiwan's ceramics capital
|journal=w:Arab News
|url=https://archive.org/details/ArabNews1983SaudiArabiaEnglish/Feb%2005%201983%2C%20Arab%20News%2C%20%2369%2C%20Saudi%20Arabia%20%28en%29/
|volume=VIII
|issue=69
|location=Saudi Arabia
|issn=0254-833X
|oclc=4574467
|page=18
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/ArabNews1983SaudiArabiaEnglish/Feb%2005%201983%2C%20Arab%20News%2C%20%2369%2C%20Saudi%20Arabia%20%28en%29/page/n17/
|column=4
|text=YINGKO – This small township in the southwest of Taipei county is not known for its beautiful scenery or historic relics. Yet every week it attracts hundreds of visitors. They all come to appreciate the '''exquisite''' pottery made in the town, for Yingko is the ceramics capital of Taiwan.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Carefully adjusted; precise; accurate; exact.
# [[recherché|Recherché]]; [[far-fetched]]; [[abstruse]].
# Of special [[beauty]] or rare [[excellence]].
# Exceeding; extreme; keen, in a bad or a good sense.
#: {{ux|en|'''exquisite''' pain or pleasure}}
# Of delicate perception or close and accurate discrimination; not easy to satisfy; exact; fastidious.
#: {{ux|en|'''exquisite''' judgment, taste, or discernment}}
#* {{RQ:Fuller Church History
|passage=his books of Oriental languages, wherein he was '''exquisite'''}}

